'''''Ruellia makoyana''''', the '''monkey plant''' or '''trailing velvet plant''', is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Acanthaceae]], [[native plant|native]] to Brazil. It is an [[evergreen]] [[perennial plant|perennial]] growing to {{convert|60|cm|0|abbr=on}} tall by {{convert|45|cm|0|abbr=on}} wide, with white-veined hairy leaves and trumpet-shaped pink flowers in summer.<ref name=RHSAZ>{{cite book|title=RHS A-Z encyclopedia of garden plants|year=2008|publisher=Dorling Kindersley|location=United Kingdom|isbn=978-1405332965|page=1136}}</ref>

With a minimum temperature of {{convert|12|C|F|abbr=on}}, in [[temperateness|temperate]] regions ''R. makoyana'' is grown indoors as a [[houseplant]]. It has gained the [[Royal Horticultural Society]]'s [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://apps.rhs.org.uk/plantselector/plant?plantid=5606 |title=RHS Plant Selector Ruellia makoyana AGM / RHS Gardening |publisher=Apps.rhs.org.uk |date= |accessdate=2013-06-16}}</ref>

